KZ2 patch 6076: LD_VP_GEN, the vertex program's identity from write stamps instead of a byte
compare. Default off; LD_VP_GEN=1 on, LD_VP_GEN=verify computes as before on every hit and compares.

Root cause ([perf-psokey]): get_pso finds the vertex program's length by scanning for its END instruction,
then compares the whole program (up to 8.5 KB) with a one-entry memo on every draw, and on a miss (the previous draw
used another program: ~30 % of draws in b-walk's heavy view, memo hits 27.8 k of ~40 k draws/s) hashes it again
(FNV) and rescans it for TXL units; vp 8.7 ms/s plus part of pre and units in the heavy view.

The transform program store (rsx_dispatch.vp) is host memory written only by rsx_dispatch.c: the upload method window,
rsx_dispatch_seed_transform_program and rsx_dispatch_init (checked by grep over libs/ and runtime/ in an earlier change:
every other use reads). Each of these now stamps the 16-instruction blocks whose words changed with a new value of
one monotonic 64-bit clock (rsx_dsp_vp_clock; an upload of an equal word stamps nothing; init and seed stamp all).
rsx_vp_gen.h keeps 16 entries by start slot (length, FNV hash, TXL mask, the clock when computed); an entry is used
only while no block of [start, start + length) carries a newer stamp, so it describes exactly the words the
computation read. A reliable write signal, not a guess: there is no other writer. The PSO key, the hash and the
shader inputs are unchanged (the memo returns the values the old code computes); [vp-gen] hits/puts/stale/bad every
65,536 draws. Test: tools/runtime/test_vp_gen.sh (the header with the patched rsx_dispatch.c: repeat, equal-word
re-upload, writes outside, changed word inside, seed, init, and a 200,000-step random stress with no false hit;
negative control TEST_NEG=1: a memo keyed by start alone gives false hits).

Written for Project Pyrrhus (KZ2 runtime); no outside code.

